[stderr] +## GPI-011 — results and local milestone contract
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Result states
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| State | Trigger and required stored fields | Available actions | Milestone effect |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `in_progress` | A run with frozen content/rules, score events, and a current safe boundary. | Resume, pause, abandon, return home only through a safe boundary. | None. |
[stderr] +| `completed_result` | Last resolved attempt is continued; immutable `ResultSummary` has `runId`, `completionId`, answered, correct, score, best active-session streak, category, outcome counts, and action labels. | Replay (new run), choose theme, exit, reopen result. | Tutorial only: request `first_whistle_complete`. |
[stderr] +| `abandoned_result` | Explicit abandon; immutable partial summary has the same fields plus `endedReason=abandoned`. | Resume only if a compatible safe snapshot precedes abandonment; otherwise replay, choose theme, exit, reopen result. | None. |
[stderr] +| `recovery` | Draft is corrupt/incompatible or a write was interrupted; last confirmed snapshot is retained. | Resume confirmed, discard draft, return home. | None until a real completion commits. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`answered` counts immutable resolved attempts. `correct` counts only `correct`.
[stderr] +`score` and `bestActiveSessionStreak` copy the committed score-event ledger.
[stderr] +The summary identifies the frozen category, not a current theme label that may
[stderr] +change. It displays score, answered/correct, best active-session streak,
[stderr] +category, and labelled replay/choose-theme/exit actions. It has no rank, RPG
[stderr] +level, loot, social comparison, or account dependency.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Completion and milestone idempotence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Completion is a single atomic logical operation keyed by `(runId, completionId)`:
[stderr] +write/retrieve the immutable `ResultSummary`, write/retrieve its aggregate
[stderr] +history entry, and, only for a completed tutorial, write/retrieve
[stderr] +`first_whistle_complete`. A duplicate command with that key returns the stored
[stderr] +objects unchanged. A completion command for a different run ID is not a retry;
[stderr] +it may create a distinct result and, for another tutorial run, returns the
[stderr] +existing milestone rather than a second one.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The `first_whistle_complete` milestone is a presence state keyed to the local
[stderr] +profile, not a counter. Its first stored value includes the source tutorial
[stderr] +run/completion ID and completion timestamp. Later tutorial completions may add
[stderr] +their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance
[stderr] +fields or create another milestone. Reopen, restart, failed UI acknowledgement,
[stderr] +and recovery replay are reads unless they initiate a new run.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Result and lifecycle fixtures
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state and idempotence result |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-01` | Complete a standard 10-card run, then reopen using its run/completion ID. | One `completed_result`, history entry, and score ledger are stored; reopen returns them without any duplicate completion or milestone. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-02` | Complete `tutorial-v1` TUT-05, then repeat completion after restart with the same IDs. | Exactly one result/history entry and one profile `first_whistle_complete` presence state; retry returns both unchanged. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-03` | Explicitly abandon after card 4, restart, and open its result. | One `abandoned_result`, zero-point abandon event, and no completion milestone; partial score/history is recoverable and no attempt is inferred for card 5. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-04` | Pause at an unresolved card, background/terminate, restart, then resume and complete. | Restore the confirmed unresolved card with no abandon/blank/timeout event; later completion creates one result and eligible tutorial milestone only once. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-05` | On final-card completion, result write is interrupted; restart with a valid prior confirmed snapshot and corrupt draft. | Enter `recovery`, retain snapshot, offer resume-confirmed/discard-draft/return-home; no result or milestone is claimed until a successful completion commits. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-06` | Complete a tutorial, confirm deletion of local history/profile/snapshots, restart, and complete a new tutorial run. | Deletion returns to first launch and removes old local records only after confirmation; the new profile/run can create one new result and one new milestone, with no duplicate residual completion. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Release boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Release validation requires `SCORE-FX-01`–`SCORE-FX-12` and
[stderr] +`RESULT-FX-01`–`RESULT-FX-06`: exactly 18 fixtures. Wrong, blank, enabled
[stderr] +timeout, and explicit abandon are all recoverable outcomes with a monotonic
[stderr] +score and no duplicate completion. Pause, interruption, and recovery are not
[stderr] +substitutes for those outcomes and cannot silently manufacture an attempt.
