[stderr] +change. It displays score, answered/correct, best active-session streak,
[stderr] +category, and labelled replay/choose-theme/exit actions. It has no rank, RPG
[stderr] +level, loot, social comparison, or account dependency.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Completion and milestone idempotence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Completion is a single atomic logical operation keyed by `(runId, completionId)`:
[stderr] +write/retrieve the immutable `ResultSummary`, write/retrieve its aggregate
[stderr] +history entry, and, only for a completed tutorial, write/retrieve
[stderr] +`first_whistle_complete`. A duplicate command with that key returns the stored
[stderr] +objects unchanged. A completion command for a different run ID is not a retry;
[stderr] +it may create a distinct result and, for another tutorial run, returns the
[stderr] +existing milestone rather than a second one.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The `first_whistle_complete` milestone is a presence state keyed to the local
[stderr] +profile, not a counter. Its first stored value includes the source tutorial
[stderr] +run/completion ID and completion timestamp. Later tutorial completions may add
[stderr] +their own immutable history/result once, but cannot replace those provenance
[stderr] +fields or create another milestone. Reopen, restart, failed UI acknowledgement,
[stderr] +and recovery replay are reads unless they initiate a new run.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +### Result and lifecycle fixtures
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Input / action | Expected deterministic state and idempotence result |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-01` | Complete a standard 10-card run, then reopen using its run/completion ID. | One `completed_result`, history entry, and score ledger are stored; reopen returns them without any duplicate completion or milestone. |
[stderr] +| `RESULT-FX-02` | Complete `tutorial-v1` TUT-05, then repeat completion after restart with the same IDs. | Exactly one result/history entry and one profile `first_whistle_complete` presence state; retry returns both unchanged. |
