gn-bible.md-46-| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-47-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-48-| GAME-005 | **Round \u201cFirst Whistle.\u201d** Tutorial round contains 5 fixed, original tutorial cards (`TUT-01`\u2013`TUT-05`) covering selecting, typing, feedback, explanation, and pause/save. It is intentionally non-timed. | This is the complete first useful journey. Completion creates/updates local milestone `first_whistle_complete`; it cannot require account, network, purchase, or deferred content. Test: a new local profile can complete it offline and resume after app restart. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-49-| GAME-006 | **Round \u201cMixed Fixture.\u201d** A 10-card themed round draws from one selected category or the Kickoff Mix, with no more than two adjacent cards sharing format or difficulty. The player may pause; a displayed timer mode is optional and defaults off. | First release ships one tutorial and one configurable standard round template, no ranked/daily/live/event modes. Test: deterministic seed produces ten eligible cards and valid format alternation or records the shortage. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:50:| GAME-007 | **Scoring and streak.** Correct = 100 points; a consecutive-correct streak of 3+ adds 25 points to each later correct answer, capped at +100. Incorrect, timeout (only if enabled), blank submission, or abandon resets the active streak; score never decreases. Explanation is available after resolution. | No paid boosts, leaderboard, social comparison, or opaque difficulty multiplier. Test: table-driven sequence proves cap, reset, and per-attempt result; a retry is a new run, not an overwrite of history. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:51:| GAME-008 | **Result and return.** Results show answered/correct, score, best active-session streak, category, and next action: replay, choose theme, or exit. Progress is local milestones and aggregate history only, not RPG levels. | An interrupted run persists at a safe boundary before the next unresolved question. Completed result is idempotent: reopening cannot award twice. Test: complete/reopen, abandon/resume, corrupted draft, and delete-history paths are specified. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-52-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-53-**Dependencies:** GAME-005 needs published tutorial cards and persistence;\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:54:GAME-006 needs GAME-001\u2013004; GAME-007 consumes adjudication events; GAME-008\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:55:consumes score events and save/recovery. Visual family is bold category panels,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-56-neutral answer controls, and non-colour success/error indicators; audio is\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-57-supportive, optional, and captioned.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-58-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-59-### Accessible, recoverable multi-target experience \u2014 `GAME-009` to `GAME-012`\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-65-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-66-| Unit | Design card / rule | First-release boundary and acceptance |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-67-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-68-| GAME-009 | **Guided start.** First launch offers an accessible plain-language tutorial entry, settings access, and a local profile without sign-in. Controls map select/navigate/confirm/back/pause to touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad. | No mandatory account. Permission denial for optional notifications/diagnostics changes no game path and explains how to alter it later. Test: every critical action is operable with keyboard and touch, focus is visible, and gamepad has an equivalent mapping. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:69:| GAME-010 | **Save/recovery.** Save immutable confirmed snapshots at tutorial completion, resolved question boundaries, explicit pause, and completed results. On failed write, retain the last confirmed snapshot and show retry/continue-without-saving. On corrupt draft, offer last confirmed snapshot or discard draft; never silently overwrite. | Remote sync/conflict requires approval and is excluded. Local deletion requires confirmation, names its effect, clears local profile/history/snapshots, and returns to first launch. Test: write failure, crash/restart, corrupt draft, and deletion fixtures preserve stated invariants. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-70-| GAME-011 | **Offline/update/error.** The installed content batch and current snapshot remain playable offline. A new content version is staged between rounds; an incompatible cache reports recovery steps and preserves confirmed save before cache reset. Unexpected errors show a plain-language retry/return-home path and optional minimised diagnostic consent. | No background live content requirement. Test: offline launch with cached assets, update mid-round, unavailable content, and diagnostic permission-denied behaviours are covered. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-71-| GAME-012 | **Platform adaptation.** Shared rule/content/save semantics on responsive web, PWA, Android, and iOS. Web adds pointer/keyboard/gamepad and responsive layouts; PWA adds install/offline cache/update UX; phones add touch targets and approved portrait/landscape choice. | No target-exclusive questions or rule differences. OS/browser matrix, orientation, performance, battery, thermal, size, store/privacy declarations, crash vendor, and exact language set remain approval gates. Test: capability matrix is exercised once targets are chosen. |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-72-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-73-Accessibility applies to all three systems: text-size and contrast settings,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:74:reduced motion, captions/text equivalents, non-colour result encoding, focus\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-75-order, semantic labels, sufficient touch targets, and no time limit by default.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-76-Localisation inputs are externalised prompt, answer, explanation, category, and\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-77-UI strings; only a future approved language may add translated content after\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-78-answer aliases and factual review are validated.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-79-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-80-**Experience production package:** a finite first-release package contains the\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-81-five named tutorial cards, one settings/help copy set, input-action labels,\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:82:result/recovery/empty-state strings, category visual tokens, and five original\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-83-optional cue families. Its workflow is interaction specification \u2192 accessible\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-84-copy/caption and focus review \u2192 original art/audio production \u2192 target\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-85-adaptation \u2192 keyboard/touch/gamepad and offline/recovery acceptance checks.\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-86-It depends on the shared shell, settings, persistence, renderer, and target\n--\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-90-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-91-| Units | First-release journeys | Implementation domains |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-92-| --- | --- | --- |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-93-| GAME-001\u2013004 | J1/J2/J4 (and J5 for versioned batch) | B content/adjudication; F delivery for batch lifecycle |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md:94:| GAME-005\u2013008 | J1/J2/J3 | A shell/progress; C rules/score/feedback; D persistence for return |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-95-| GAME-009\u2013012 | J0/J1/J2/J3/J5 | D recovery, E accessibility/input/presentation, F delivery/targets |\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-96-\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-97-The machine-readable `implementation_map` in the companion JSON maps every\nprojects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.md-98-individual `GAME-*` unit, rather than treating this grouped table as a substitute.\n\nexec\n/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,130p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.md; sed -n '1,150p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/planning/game-production-inventory.json; sed -n '1,130p' projects/football-trivia-e2e/specification/02-game-design-bible.json\" in /Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator\n succeeded in 0ms:\n# Game production inventory\n\n**Source:** `specification/02-game-design-bible.json`. This inventory i